A1. `MemberUseScanner` — RETAINED BYTE-FOR-BYTE. Owns calls, `new`, property/field reads, method groups. `Register(CompilationStartAnalysisContext, Action<OperationAnalysisContext, ISymbol, INamedTypeSymbol>)` at `MemberUseScanner.cs:43` and `RegisterForAssembly(...)` at `:61`. Consumed by AG0040 (Engine gate), AG0041 (both consumer gates), and AG0023/AG0029 (Boundaries gate unchanged + new Engine gate). Reuse, not extract: `RegisterForAssembly` returns without registering when the compilation is not the named assembly, so a rule calls it once per gate.

A2. `DeclaredTypeScanner` — EXTRACT from `ContractConcreteTypeMustNotBeReferencedAnalyzer.cs:49-52` (the four registrations) and `:55-102` (the four handlers). Owns "the types a symbol carries without naming them".

```csharp
internal readonly struct DeclaredTypeUse
{
    internal DeclaredTypeUse(ITypeSymbol type, Location location, ISymbol containingSymbol, Action<Diagnostic> report)
    { Type = type; Location = location; ContainingSymbol = containingSymbol; Report = report; }

    internal ITypeSymbol Type { get; }
    internal Location Location { get; }
    internal ISymbol ContainingSymbol { get; }   // the caller-site symbol AG0023/AG0029 test the door against
    internal Action<Diagnostic> Report { get; }  // SymbolAnalysisContext and OperationAnalysisContext share no base
}

internal static class DeclaredTypeScanner
{
    internal static readonly ImmutableArray<SymbolKind> DeclarationKinds =
        ImmutableArray.Create(SymbolKind.Field, SymbolKind.Property, SymbolKind.Method);

    internal static void Register(CompilationStartAnalysisContext context, Action<DeclaredTypeUse> inspect)
    {
        context.RegisterSymbolAction(c => DispatchSymbol(c, inspect), DeclarationKinds);
        context.RegisterOperationAction(c => DispatchLocal(c, inspect), OperationKind.VariableDeclarator);
    }

    internal static void RegisterForAssembly(
        CompilationStartAnalysisContext context, string assemblyName, Action<DeclaredTypeUse> inspect)
    {
        if (!string.Equals(context.Compilation.AssemblyName, assemblyName, StringComparison.Ordinal)) return;
        Register(context, inspect);
    }

    // The judgment, pure and directly callable — this is what the direct scanner tests drive.
    internal static IEnumerable<(ITypeSymbol Type, Location Location)> CarriedTypes(ISymbol symbol)
    {
        switch (symbol)
        {
            case IFieldSymbol { IsImplicitlyDeclared: false } field when field.Locations.Length > 0:
                yield return (field.Type, field.Locations[0]); break;
            case IPropertySymbol { IsImplicitlyDeclared: false } property when property.Locations.Length > 0:
                yield return (property.Type, property.Locations[0]); break;
            case ILocalSymbol local when local.Locations.Length > 0:
                yield return (local.Type, local.Locations[0]); break;
            case IMethodSymbol method when !method.IsImplicitlyDeclared && !IsAccessor(method):
                if (method.Locations.Length > 0) yield return (method.ReturnType, method.Locations[0]);
                foreach (var parameter in method.Parameters)
                    if (parameter.Locations.Length > 0) yield return (parameter.Type, parameter.Locations[0]);
                break;
        }
    }

    private static bool IsAccessor(IMethodSymbol method) =>
        method.MethodKind is MethodKind.PropertyGet or MethodKind.PropertySet
            or MethodKind.EventAdd or MethodKind.EventRemove or MethodKind.EventRaise;

    private static void DispatchSymbol(SymbolAnalysisContext context, Action<DeclaredTypeUse> inspect)
    {
        foreach ((ITypeSymbol type, Location location) in CarriedTypes(context.Symbol))
            inspect(new DeclaredTypeUse(type, location, context.Symbol, context.ReportDiagnostic));
    }

    private static void DispatchLocal(OperationAnalysisContext context, Action<DeclaredTypeUse> inspect)
    {
        var declarator = (IVariableDeclaratorOperation)context.Operation;
        foreach ((ITypeSymbol type, Location location) in CarriedTypes(declarator.Symbol))
            inspect(new DeclaredTypeUse(type, location, context.ContainingSymbol, context.ReportDiagnostic));
    }
}
```

AG0006's `Initialize` becomes one line: `context.RegisterCompilationStartAction(start => DeclaredTypeScanner.Register(start, Inspect));` where `Inspect` applies its existing `ContractPattern.ReferencesContractImplementation` leaf test and reports `Rule`. The four handlers and their per-position locations disappear into `CarriedTypes`; every reported location is identical (method location for a bad return type, parameter location for a bad parameter, `locations[0]` for field/property, `Symbol.Locations[0]` for a local).

