G. DIRECT SCANNER TESTS
====================================================================

MEASURED BLOCKER: a `DiagnosticAnalyzer` **cannot be declared in `AgentGuard.Analyzers.Tests`**. A project mirroring its exact package set on net10.0 with `TreatWarningsAsErrors=true` fails the build with four errors — RS1038 (references `Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.Workspaces`), RS1041 (target framework net10.0), RS1036 (`EnforceExtendedAnalyzerRules`), RS2008 (release tracking). `Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.Analyzers/3.11.0` is in that project's asset graph and there is no RS relaxation in `eng/agentguard-test-analyzer-relaxations.globalconfig`. So the "probe analyzer in the test project" design is not buildable, and suppressing four RS rules to make it buildable is weakening a check to avoid work.

That is why both scanners expose a pure `Resolve`/`CarriedTypes`. The tests drive them through `AnalyzerRunner.CompileAsync`, which exists for exactly this and says so — "so a test can drive an internal helper (for example `BoundaryServices.Resolve`) directly" — with `DerivedBoundaryServicesTests.cs` as the live precedent. `AgentGuard.Analyzers.csproj` already grants `InternalsVisibleTo("AgentGuard.Analyzers.Tests")`.

`WrittenNameScannerTests.cs` selects nodes with `WrittenNameScanner.NameKinds.Contains(node.Kind())` — the same field `Register` hands Roslyn, so narrowing the kind list turns the direct test red too. Cases: every contract-named position (`typeof`, `nameof`, cast, `is` pattern, generic type argument, generic constraint, base list, attribute argument, using alias and its use, array element, pointer target, field/property/parameter/return/local declaration, inferred `var`); the generic guarded type `GuardedG<int>` written WITH arguments, whose only node is the `GenericName` (its identifier is a token, not a child `IdentifierName`); member names (`Create`, a field, a property, a method group); and the unresolved-symbol cases — the four malformed-attribute spellings that must come back through tier 2, and a genuinely undefined identifier that must come back `(null, null)` and be dropped.

`DeclaredTypeScannerTests.cs` drives `CarriedTypes` over each symbol kind and asserts the type AND the location: method location for the return type, parameter location for a parameter, `locations[0]` for field/property/local, nothing for implicitly declared members and property/event accessors.

